{
"content_id": "27191",
"reference_id": 26333,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Vashti",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "vashti",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<h2>Definition:</h2>\n<p>In the Old Testament book of Esther, Vashti was the wife of Ahasuerus, king of Persia.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>King Ahasuerus sent Queen Vashti away when she refused to obey his order to come to his dinner party and show off her beauty to his drunken guests.</li>\n<li>As a result, a search went out for a new queen and eventually Esther was chosen to be the king’s new wife.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>(Translation suggestions: Translate Names)</p>\n<p>(See also: <span data-bnType=\"resourceReference\" data-resourceId=\"25439\" data-resourceType=\"UWTranslationWords\">Ahasuerus</span>, <span data-bnType=\"resourceReference\" data-resourceId=\"25711\" data-resourceType=\"UWTranslationWords\">Esther</span>, <span data-bnType=\"resourceReference\" data-resourceId=\"26091\" data-resourceType=\"UWTranslationWords\">Persia</span>)</p>\n<h2>Bible References:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Esther 1:9–11</li>\n<li>Esther 2:1–2</li>\n<li>Esther 2:17–18</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Word Data:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Strong’s: H2060</li>\n</ul>",
